# Codex PLAN review — P8C Frontend semantic resolver (disclaude). See "## PR P8C" in disclaude.md.

The frontend ALREADY has selectionAgent.ts + selectionBridge.ts (SourceRef from data-oid) + click-to-edit
(EditAffordance/PreviewPane). P8C adds a pure data-disco-* → typed-target resolver with a data-oid fallback, plus
a TS constants file (discoSemanticAttrs.ts) kept in parity with Python core DataDiscoAttr (P8B) by a Python
drift-guard test. The resolver walks the DOM up from a clicked element by priority field>section>file>
comment_anchor>data-oid, and a field target also captures its enclosing section so "click hero headline" yields
{section:'hero',field:'headline'}.

Judge: (a) is the priority order (field > section > file > comment_anchor > data-oid-source) correct, and is
"field also captures enclosing section" the right way to produce app_update_content(hero.headline)? (b) is the TS-
constants + Python-drift-guard the right single-source mechanism across the language boundary, or should P8B have
generated the .ts? (c) the result discriminated union mirroring P8A locators — should the SOURCE fallback be a
distinct kind ('source') vs the semantic kinds, and is mixing them in one resolver sound? (d) is deferring the
actual in-frame selectionAgent injection + live click to P1B-LIVE acceptable (keeping P8C as the pure unit-tested
resolver), or must P8C wire selectionAgent now? (e) scope/risks. Return APPROVE|REVISE|BLOCKED + REASONS +
REQUIRED_REVISIONS.
